<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dinner Picker | Random Meal Decision Tool</title><meta name="description" content="Can't decide what to eat? Add meal ideas or use the starter list, then randomly choose dinner. Free browser-based meal decision tool."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="canonical" href="https://wheelnamepicker.com.au/dinner-picker"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/value-pages.css"></head><body><div class="top"><div class="nav"><a class="brand" href="/">Wheel Name Picker</a><div class="links"><a href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker</a><a href="/chore-picker">Chore Picker</a><a href="/yes-no-picker">Yes/No Picker</a></div></div></div><header class="hero"><span class="badge">Decision helper</span><h1>Dinner Picker</h1><p>When everyone has answered “I don't know”, put the realistic meal options in one list and let the picker choose. Edit the starter ideas to match what is actually available tonight.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="tool"><div class="grid"><div class="field"><label for="meals">Meal ideas</label><textarea id="meals">Tacos
Stir-fry
Pasta
Homemade burgers
Baked potatoes
Curry
Soup and toast
Chicken wraps</textarea></div><div class="field"><label for="remove">After picking</label><select id="remove"><option value="keep">Keep all meals</option><option value="remove">Remove the chosen meal</option></select><div class="actions"><button id="pick">Pick dinner</button><button class="secondary" id="quick">Load quick-budget ideas</button></div></div></div><div class="result big-choice" id="result">What's for dinner?</div></div><div class="article"><section><h2>Use the options you really have</h2><p>The dinner picker is most useful when the list reflects your actual pantry, energy and time. Remove anything that needs ingredients you do not have, and add leftovers, takeaway options or simple meals that suit the night. Random choice works better after impossible options have already been filtered out.</p></section><section><h2>A quick way to reduce decision fatigue</h2><p>Meal decisions can become strangely expensive in mental energy when several people are hungry and every suggestion gets rejected. A short list with four to eight acceptable options turns the problem from “invent dinner” into “accept one of these reasonable choices”. The picker handles only the final tie-break.</p></section><section><h2>Build different lists for different nights</h2><ul><li><strong>Fast nights:</strong> wraps, eggs on toast, pasta, leftovers, soup or toasted sandwiches.</li><li><strong>Cook-from-scratch nights:</strong> curry, tray bake, stir-fry, tacos or homemade pizza.</li><li><strong>Low-cost nights:</strong> baked potatoes, lentil dishes, rice bowls, omelettes or pantry pasta.</li><li><strong>Family-choice nights:</strong> ask each person to add one realistic option, then pick from the combined list.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Food needs come before randomness</h2><p>Do not include foods that are unsuitable because of allergies, medical dietary requirements, choking risk or other safety needs. The picker does not evaluate nutrition, ingredients or food safety. It simply chooses from the options you supply.</p></section><section><h2>Privacy and saving</h2><p>The meal list is handled in your browser and does not require an account. If you want to keep a favourite list for future nights, copy it into your notes app. The page intentionally avoids collecting a profile of what you eat.</p></section></div></main><footer class="footer"><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><p>© 2026 Wheel Name Picker · Ascension Digital Group</p></footer><script>const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),budget='Baked potatoes\nEggs on toast\nVegetable fried rice\nPasta with tomato sauce\nSoup and toast\nBean tacos\nOmelette\nLeftovers';function list(){return $('meals').value.split(/\n|,/).map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean)}$('pick').onclick=()=>{const a=list();if(!a.length)return $('result').textContent='Add at least one meal idea.';const i=Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length),v=a[i];$('result').textContent=v;if($('remove').value==='remove'){a.splice(i,1);$('meals').value=a.join('\n')}};$('quick').onclick=()=>{$('meals').value=budget;$('result').textContent='Budget-friendly list loaded'};</script></body></html>